      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "Doctors Without Borders demonstrates a high capacity for rapid mobilization, supported by <cite id=\"1\">$767,362,916 in FY2023 revenue</cite>. Their financial model is built for resilience, evidenced by <cite id=\"1\">3.7 months of working capital</cite> that allows them to act without waiting for specific grant approvals. This independence is further bolstered by a <cite id=\"1\">91% independent board</cite>, ensuring that governance remains focused on the medical mission. Their operational efficiency is notable; they achieve a <cite id=\"1\">100/100 score for Leadership</cite> from Charity Navigator while keeping <cite id=\"1\">fundraising costs at just $0.15 per $1 raised</cite>."
      ],
      "summary": "Doctors Without Borders USA (MSF) operates as a massive humanitarian engine, providing <cite id=\"4\">critical medical care during wars</cite> and natural disasters. In FY2024, the organization reported <cite id=\"3\">total revenue of $776,922,926</cite>, reflecting its status as a primary global responder. The charity maintains a <cite id=\"1\">97/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite>, which signals high levels of trust and operational transparency. While the organization is <cite id=\"2\">sadaqah-eligible</cite>, it serves as a vital channel for Muslim donors to support humanitarian relief in <cite id=\"2\">Muslim-majority regions</cite> facing crisis. MSF is distinguished by its <cite id=\"6\">direct service delivery model</cite>, which includes performing thousands of <cite id=\"5\">surgeries in disaster zones</cite> and managing infectious disease outbreaks. Financial health remains a core strength, as the charity holds <cite id=\"1\">3.7 months of working capital</cite> in working capital. This reserve allows for immediate mobilization when new emergencies arise. Despite its scale, MSF maintains <cite id=\"1\">strong fundraising efficiency</cite>, spending only <cite id=\"1\">$0.15 to raise every $1</cite>. This ensures that the vast majority of contributions are directed toward medical supplies and field staff rather than administrative overhead.",
